        --[[
            The keeper's vial: sap that has gone to glass with a light
            still in it, caged in iron and hung off a thong.

            This is the object the archive has been describing for twenty
            fragments. He tapped the Sapglass Grove and left the vials
            full, which is not what a thief does, and what was in them was
            a memory being held somewhere other than a lantern. He has
            carried this one since.

            Two things make it his rather than another lamp. It is caged
            the way the mireglass shard is, because glass with no edge
            photographs as a smear -- and the core is Neon and nothing in
            the game tells it to breathe. Every other light in Emberhollow
            is on the ambient controller and flickers. This one does not,
            which is the exact sentence the fragment uses.
        ]]
