        --[[
            A trap standing set, held open, the size of two hands. She
            built them for a road that no longer needs them and she is
            building them anyway, smaller.

            Face-on rather than flat, because a jaw trap lying flat is a
            disc and a jaw trap open is a ring with teeth in it, which is
            a shape nothing else in this cast makes. The jaws are two arcs
            with the gaps at top and bottom, so the thing reads as parted
            rather than closed.

            The first pass photographed as a gear with a brass hub: the
            teeth sat at the same radius as the jaws and disappeared into
            them, and a pale pan in the middle took the eye. Teeth are the
            whole difference between a trap and a wheel, so they stand
            well inside the ring now, in bright steel, crossing into the
            open middle where there is nothing behind them -- and the pan
            went dark, because a gap wants to read as a gap.
        ]]
