            photographed as a bolt with nuts run down it. A cord only
            reads as a cord if it is not straight: these three drape, each
            kinking against the last, and the weight below is one long
            ellipsoid rather than a stack of discs, because a plumb bob is
            a teardrop and a stack of discs is machined.

            Cass carries a ring of rope; this is the opposite shape on
            purpose, since what a sounding line says is depth. The two rag
            ties are fathom marks and the tip is armed with tallow, so the
            lead comes back up wearing whatever the bottom is made of. She
            has never said what came up on it.
