            The Crown's four came out of a city that kept performing its
            own ceremonies while it burned, and each of them answered that
            by doing the same job honestly. Sabine cast people for the
            Crown and will not cast anything shaped like a person now.
            Theo copied the official names for thirty years and started
            copying the scratched-out ones too. Delia knows which of the
            Crown's statues were people, and says so at length to anyone
            who asks and to nobody when nobody does. Bran cut beams for a
            city that burned anyway.

            The Hollow's four are the postgame and arrive with chapter
            seven, so most players will never see them and the ones who do
            have finished the game. That is the reason they are worth
            authoring rather than deriving: a town that is visibly
            different afterwards is the whole reward, and eight identical
            coats standing on a ring around the plaza is not a different
            town.

            Same rules as the sixteen above. Day is the building the
            roster gives them the job at -- the glassworks, the records
            office, the memorial hall, the sawmill, the lamp house, the
            deep well, the meeting hall, the trapworks. Dusk is that
            person's own last hour. Night is the lantern road, and it now
            carries all twenty-seven down its length.
